  },
  "markdown": "# Communication and Active Listening Techniques\n- Video/PDF\n  - 1. What is Communication?\n    - Process of exchanging information, ideas, and emotions\n    - Includes Verbal (spoken/written) + Non-verbal (body language, facial expressions, tone, gestures)\n    - Goal: Message is understood as intended\n    - Key Components: Cyclical process (Feedback is essential)\n      - Sender → Message → Medium → Receiver → Feedback\n  - 2. Barriers to Effective Communication\n    - Language differences\n    - Cultural misunderstandings\n    - Personal biases\n    - Solution: Awareness + Adaptability + Inclusive approach\n  - 3. Features of Effective Communication (in Career Counselling)\n    - 1. Create a Safe Space\n      - Physical: Private, comfortable, minimal distractions\n      - Emotional: Trust, empathy, non-judgmental acceptance\n      - Confidentiality assurance\n      - Sensitivity to cultural & individual differences\n    - 2. Establish Proper Context\n      - Explain purpose of session\n      - Discuss client's goals & expectations\n      - Address questions & concerns\n      - Create collaborative environment\n    - 3. Use Empathy\n      - Deeply understand & validate client's feelings\n      - Reflect emotions (e.g., \"It sounds like you're feeling overwhelmed…\")\n      - Use open-ended questions to explore deeper\n      - Builds therapeutic alliance & encourages honesty\n    - 4. Encourage Client Input\n      - Ask open-ended questions & invite feedback\n      - Collaborative strategy discussion\n      - Respect client's autonomy\n      - Maintain professional boundaries\n    - 5. Follow-up, Summarize & Reflect\n      - Follow-up: Review progress, assignments, challenges\n      - Summarize: Condense key points + clarify next steps\n      - Reflect: Evaluate session (counsellor + client)\n      - Helps adjust plan & maintain momentum\n  - 4. Active Listening Techniques (Prime Component in Career Counselling)\n    - 1. Reflective Listening\n      - Mirror back what client said + validate feelings\n    - 2. Open-Ended Questions\n      - Encourage detailed responses (cannot answer with Yes/No)\n    - 3. Paraphrasing\n      - Restate client's points in your own words for clarity\n    - 4. Non-Verbal Cues\n      - Nodding, eye contact, leaning forward\n      - Shows full engagement\n    - 5. Avoiding Interruptions\n      - Give client full space to express thoughts\n- Quiz\n",
